-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/47bd0b90-2b4f-44bf-9364-289e265d7cff
-- title:
--   The load-balancing model (§2.1), scaling and critical load (2.9)–(2.13), (IC₀), data (2.17) and $(\hat X^n,\hat L^n)$ (2.14)
-- statement:
--   This file defines a **sequence of load-balancing systems**, indexed by $n\in\mathbb N$, all on one probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$. Each system has $N$ queues and servers and $N+1$ arrival streams. For the $n$-th system and $i\in[N]$:
--
--   1. **Arrivals.** $E^n_i$ and $A^n_0$ are Poisson processes of intensities $\lambda^n_i$ and $\lambda^n_0$. Stream $i$ feeds queue $i$, and $A^n_0$ is the load-balancing stream (LBS).
--   2. **Routing.** $p=(p_r)$ is a probability vector with $p_1\ge\dots\ge p_N$ (2.4). The marks $\theta_k$, $k\ge1$, are i.i.d. with $P(\theta_1=r)=p_r$. The $k$-th LBS arrival, at time $t^n(k)=\inf\{t\ge0: A^n_0(t)\ge k\}$, joins the queue whose rank just before the arrival equals $\theta_k$:
--
--   $$
--   A^n_i(t)=\int_{[0,t]}1_{\{\mathcal R^n_i(s-)=\theta_{A^n_0(s)}\}}\,dA^n_0(s)=\sum_{k=1}^{A^n_0(t)}1_{\{\mathrm{rank}(i;X^n(t^n(k)-))=\theta_k\}} .
--   $$
--
--   3. **Service.** $\Phi^{ser}_i$ is a probability measure on $[0,\infty)$ with mean $1$, standard deviation $\sigma^{ser}_i\in(0,\infty)$ and $\Phi^{ser}_i(\{0\})=0$. The service times $Z^n_i(k)$, $k\ge1$, are i.i.d. with law $\Phi^{ser,n}_i$, where $\Phi^{ser,n}_i[0,x]=\Phi^{ser}_i[0,\mu^n_ix]$ and $\mu^n_i>0$ (2.7). The potential service process is
--
--   $$
--   S^n_i(t)=\max\Big\{k\in\mathbb Z_+:\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}Z^n_i(j)\le t\Big\} \qquad (2.8),
--   $$
--
--   where $Z^n_i(0)$ is the initial residual time.
--
--   4. **Initial condition.** The initial tuple is $\mathcal I^n=(X^n(0-),Z^n(0))$. For each $i$, either $X^n_i(0-)=1$ and $Z^n_i(0)=0$ (a fictitious job, $i\in\mathcal N^n$), or $X^n_i(0-)\ge1$ and $Z^n_i(0)>0$ ($i\in\mathcal P^n$).
--   5. **Independence.** For each $n$ the $2N+3$ elements $E^n_i$, $(Z^n_i(k))_{k\ge1}$, $\mathcal I^n$, $A^n_0$ and $\{\theta_k\}$ are mutually independent.
--   6. **Dynamics.** Almost surely, for $t\ge0$: $X^n_i(t)=X^n_i(0-)+E^n_i(t)+A^n_i(t)-D^n_i(t)$ (2.1), $T^n_i(t)=\int_0^t1_{\{X^n_i(s)>0\}}ds$ (2.2), and $D^n_i=S^n_i\circ T^n_i$. The queue lengths have càdlàg integer-valued paths.
--
--   **Scaling (§2.2).** There are constants $\lambda_i>0$, $\hat\lambda_i\in\mathbb R$, $\lambda_0>0$, $\mu_i>0$, $\hat\mu_i\in\mathbb R$ such that the following hold:
--
--   - $n^{-1/2}(\lambda^n_i-n\lambda_i)\to\hat\lambda_i$ (2.9);
--   - $n^{-1/2}\lambda^n_0\to\lambda_0$ (2.10);
--   - $n^{-1/2}(\mu^n_i-n\mu_i)\to\hat\mu_i$ (2.11);
--   - $\lambda_i=\mu_i$ (2.12, critical load);
--   - $n^{1/2}Z^n_i(0)\to0$ in probability (2.13).
--
--   **(IC₀)** holds when $\hat X^n(0-)=n^{-1/2}X^n(0-)\Rightarrow X_0$, i.e. the laws of $\hat X^n(0-)$ converge weakly to a probability measure $\mu_0$ on $\mathbb R^N$.
--
--   **Data (2.17):** $b_r=\lambda_0p_r$, $m_i=\hat\lambda_i-\hat\mu_i$, $\sigma_i=(\lambda_i+\mu_i(\sigma^{ser}_i)^2)^{1/2}$. **Scaled processes (2.14):** $\hat X^n_i(t)=n^{-1/2}X^n_i(t)$ and $\hat L^n_i(t)=n^{-1/2}\mu^n_i(t-T^n_i(t))$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The following conventions are fixed.
--
--   - Servers and ranks are `Fin N`.
--   - (2.5) is encoded as the finite sum over LBS arrival epochs, as the paper rewrites it on p. 12, with the rank taken at the left limits $X^n(t^n(k)-)$. The marks are allowed to depend on $n$ ($\theta^n_k$, as in the proof of Lemma 4.3).
--   - The processes $X,T,A,S,D$ are fields of the structure, constrained by the equations; the equations hold $P$-a.s.
--   - $S$ is real-valued and required to equal the $\mathbb N_\infty$-valued maximum (2.8), which forces it to be finite.
--   - The constants of §2.2 are fields of `HeavyTraffic`, and $b,m,\sigma$ are computed from them and from $p$ and $\Phi^{ser}$.
--   - $\sigma^{ser}_i$ is computed as $(\int(x-1)^2\,d\Phi^{ser}_i)^{1/2}$.
--   - $n^{-1/2}$ is `1/√n`; its value at $n=0$ does not affect any limit.
--   - Independence is `iIndep` of the σ-algebras generated by the $2N+3$ elements.
-- source:
--   Atar & Ichiba, Rank-Based Stochastic Differential Inclusions and Diffusion Limits for a Load Balancing Model, arXiv:2409.15121v1, pp. 3–6, §2.1 (2.1)–(2.8), §2.2 (2.9)–(2.14), (IC₀); p. 8, (2.17); p. 12, rewriting of (2.5)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_BellWilliams2001_ThresholdPolicy_Paths
import Definitions.Def_RankBasedSDI_LoadBalancing_Rank
import Definitions.Def_RankBasedSDI_LoadBalancing_PoissonProcess

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

namespace RankBasedSDI.LoadBalancing

open BellWilliams2001.ThresholdPolicy

/-!
Atar & Ichiba, arXiv:2409.15121v1, §2.1–2.2 and (2.17), pp. 3–8: the sequence of load-balancing
systems, the scaling and critical-load conditions, the initial condition (IC₀), the limit data
`(b, m, σ)` and the diffusion-scaled queue lengths and idle times (2.14).

Conventions. Servers and ranks are `Fin N` (paper index minus one). All systems live on one
probability space `(Ω, P)`, as in the paper. Time is real and only `t ≥ 0` is used.
-/

/-- The potential service process (2.8), `S(t) = max{k ∈ ℤ₊ : ∑_{j=0}^{k−1} z(j) ≤ t}`, with the
empty sum equal to `0`; the sum starts at `j = 0`, the initial residual time. It is computed in
`ℕ∞`, so it is `⊤` (never a junk finite value) if infinitely many partial sums are `≤ t`. -/
noncomputable def potentialService (z : ℕ → ℝ) (t : ℝ) : ℕ∞ :=
  ⨆ (k : ℕ) (_ : ∑ j ∈ Finset.range k, z j ≤ t), (k : ℕ∞)

/-- The `k`-th arrival epoch of a counting path, `t(k) = inf{t ≥ 0 : a(t) ≥ k}` (p. 11). It is
only used for `1 ≤ k ≤ a(t)`, where the set is nonempty and bounded below by `0`. -/
noncomputable def arrivalEpoch (a : ℝ → ℝ) (k : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  sInf {t : ℝ | 0 ≤ t ∧ (k : ℝ) ≤ a t}

/-- The routed load-balancing arrivals (2.5), written as on p. 12 as a sum over the arrival
epochs `t(k)` of the load-balancing stream `a = A₀`:
`A_i(t) = ∑_{k=1}^{A₀(t)} 1{rank(i; X(t(k)−)) = θ_k}`. The rank is taken at the left limit
`X(t(k)−)` (the state just before the arrival). -/
noncomputable def routedCount {N : ℕ} (x : Fin N → ℝ → ℝ) (a : ℝ → ℝ) (θ : ℕ → Fin N)
    (i : Fin N) (t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ k ∈ Finset.Icc 1 ⌊a t⌋₊,
    if rank (fun j => Function.leftLim (x j) (arrivalEpoch a k)) i = θ k then 1 else 0

/-- **The sequence of load-balancing systems** (§2.1, pp. 3–5), indexed by `n ∈ ℕ`, on one
probability space `(Ω, P)`. For the `n`-th system and server `i`:
* `E n i`, `A0 n` are Poisson processes of intensities `λⁿᵢ = lam n i`, `λⁿ₀ = lam0 n`;
* `θ n k` (`k ≥ 1`) are i.i.d. ranks with `P(θ = r) = p_r`, `p` a nonincreasing probability
  vector (2.4);
* `Φser i` is the service-time law (mean `1`, finite positive variance, no atom at `0`); the
  service times `Z n i k`, `k ≥ 1`, are i.i.d. with law `Φ^{ser,n}_i`, the image of `Φser i`
  under `x ↦ x / µⁿᵢ` (2.7); `Z n i 0` is the initial residual time;
* `X0m n i = Xⁿᵢ(0−) ∈ ℕ`, with `(Xⁿᵢ(0−), Zⁿᵢ(0)) = (1, 0)` (fictitious job, `i ∈ 𝒩ⁿ`) or
  `Xⁿᵢ(0−) ≥ 1, Zⁿᵢ(0) > 0` (`i ∈ 𝒫ⁿ`);
* for each `n` the `2N + 3` elements `Eⁿᵢ`, `𝒵ⁿᵢ = (Zⁿᵢ(k))_{k≥1}`, `ℐⁿ`, `Aⁿ₀`, `{θ_k}` are
  mutually independent;
* the queue length `X`, busy time `T`, routed arrivals `A`, potential service `S` and departures
  `D` satisfy, almost surely, (2.1), (2.2), (2.5), (2.8) and `D = S ∘ T`; `X` has càdlàg
  `ℕ`-valued paths. -/
structure LoadBalancingSequence (Ω : Type*) [MeasurableSpace Ω] (N : ℕ) where
  P : Measure Ω
  isProbability : IsProbabilityMeasure P
  /-- routing probabilities `p_r` (Lean index `r` is the paper's rank `r + 1`) -/
  p : Fin N → ℝ
  p_nonneg : ∀ r, 0 ≤ p r
  p_sum : ∑ r, p r = 1
  /-- (2.4): `p₁ ≥ p₂ ≥ ⋯ ≥ p_N` -/
  p_antitone : Antitone p
  /-- `θ n k`, used for `k ≥ 1` -/
  θ : ℕ → ℕ → Ω → Fin N
  θ_measurable : ∀ n k, Measurable (θ n k)
  θ_iid : ∀ n, iIndepFun (fun (k : ℕ) ω => θ n (k + 1) ω) P
  θ_law : ∀ n k (r : Fin N), P {ω | θ n (k + 1) ω = r} = ENNReal.ofReal (p r)
  /-- arrival rates `λⁿᵢ` and LBS rate `λⁿ₀`, service rates `µⁿᵢ > 0` -/
  lam : ℕ → Fin N → ℝ≥0
  lam0 : ℕ → ℝ≥0
  mu : ℕ → Fin N → ℝ
  mu_pos : ∀ n i, 0 < mu n i
  /-- service-time laws `Φ^ser_i` on `[0, ∞)` -/
  Φser : Fin N → Measure ℝ
  Φser_prob : ∀ i, IsProbabilityMeasure (Φser i)
  Φser_nonneg : ∀ i, Φser i (Set.Iio 0) = 0
  Φser_no_atom : ∀ i, Φser i {0} = 0
  Φser_sq_integrable : ∀ i, Integrable (fun x : ℝ => x ^ 2) (Φser i)
  Φser_mean : ∀ i, ∫ x, x ∂(Φser i) = 1
  Φser_var_pos : ∀ i, 0 < ∫ x, (x - 1) ^ 2 ∂(Φser i)
  /-- exogenous arrival streams `Eⁿᵢ` and the LBS stream `Aⁿ₀` -/
  E : ℕ → Fin N → Ω → ℝ → ℝ
  E_poisson : ∀ n i, IsPoissonProcess P (lam n i) (E n i)
  E_measurable : ∀ n i (t : ℝ), Measurable fun ω => E n i ω t
  A0 : ℕ → Ω → ℝ → ℝ
  A0_poisson : ∀ n, IsPoissonProcess P (lam0 n) (A0 n)
  A0_measurable : ∀ n (t : ℝ), Measurable fun ω => A0 n ω t
  /-- service times `Zⁿᵢ(k)`, `k ≥ 1`, and initial residual times `Zⁿᵢ(0)` -/
  Z : ℕ → Fin N → ℕ → Ω → ℝ
  Z_measurable : ∀ n i k, Measurable (Z n i k)
  Z_iid : ∀ n i, iIndepFun (fun (k : ℕ) ω => Z n i (k + 1) ω) P
  Z_law : ∀ n i k, HasLaw (Z n i (k + 1)) ((Φser i).map (fun x => x / mu n i)) P
  /-- initial queue lengths `Xⁿᵢ(0−)` -/
  X0m : ℕ → Fin N → Ω → ℕ
  X0m_measurable : ∀ n i, Measurable (X0m n i)
  initial : ∀ n i ω,
    (X0m n i ω = 1 ∧ Z n i 0 ω = 0) ∨ (1 ≤ X0m n i ω ∧ 0 < Z n i 0 ω)
  /-- mutual independence of `Eⁿᵢ, 𝒵ⁿᵢ (i ∈ [N]), ℐⁿ, Aⁿ₀, {θ_k}` for each `n` -/
  indep : ∀ n, iIndep (fun j : (Fin N ⊕ Fin N) ⊕ (Unit ⊕ Unit ⊕ Unit) =>
      match j with
      | .inl (.inl i) => MeasurableSpace.comap (E n i) inferInstance
      | .inl (.inr i) => MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (k : ℕ) => Z n i (k + 1) ω) inferInstance
      | .inr (.inl _) =>
          MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (i : Fin N) => ((X0m n i ω : ℝ), Z n i 0 ω)) inferInstance
      | .inr (.inr (.inl _)) => MeasurableSpace.comap (A0 n) inferInstance
      | .inr (.inr (.inr _)) =>
          MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω (k : ℕ) => θ n (k + 1) ω) inferInstance) P
  /-- the system processes -/
  X : ℕ → Fin N → Ω → ℝ → ℝ
  T : ℕ → Fin N → Ω → ℝ → ℝ
  A : ℕ → Fin N → Ω → ℝ → ℝ
  S : ℕ → Fin N → Ω → ℝ → ℝ
  D : ℕ → Fin N → Ω → ℝ → ℝ
  X_measurable : ∀ n i (t : ℝ), Measurable fun ω => X n i ω t
  T_measurable : ∀ n i (t : ℝ), Measurable fun ω => T n i ω t
  A_measurable : ∀ n i (t : ℝ), Measurable fun ω => A n i ω t
  S_measurable : ∀ n i (t : ℝ), Measurable fun ω => S n i ω t
  D_measurable : ∀ n i (t : ℝ), Measurable fun ω => D n i ω t
  X_cadlag : ∀ n i ω, IsCadlag (X n i ω)
  X_nat : ∀ n i ω (t : ℝ), 0 ≤ t → ∃ k : ℕ, X n i ω t = k
  /-- (2.1) -/
  balance : ∀ n i, ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t →
    X n i ω t = (X0m n i ω : ℝ) + E n i ω t + A n i ω t - D n i ω t
  /-- (2.2) -/
  busy : ∀ n i, ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t →
    T n i ω t = ∫ s in (0 : ℝ)..t, if 0 < X n i ω s then (1 : ℝ) else 0
  /-- (2.8): `S` is the (finite) potential service count -/
  service : ∀ n i, ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t →
    ∃ k : ℕ, S n i ω t = k ∧ potentialService (fun j => Z n i j ω) t = (k : ℕ∞)
  /-- `Dⁿᵢ(t) = Sⁿᵢ(Tⁿᵢ(t))` -/
  departures : ∀ n i, ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t → D n i ω t = S n i ω (T n i ω t)
  /-- (2.5), routing by the rank at the left limit `Xⁿ(s−)` -/
  routing : ∀ n i, ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ t →
    A n i ω t = routedCount (fun j => X n j ω) (A0 n ω) (fun k => θ n k ω) i t

variable {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {N : ℕ}

/-- **Scaling and critical load** (§2.2, pp. 5–6): constants `λᵢ > 0, λ̂ᵢ ∈ ℝ, λ₀ > 0, µᵢ > 0,
µ̂ᵢ ∈ ℝ` with (2.9) `n^{−1/2}(λⁿᵢ − nλᵢ) → λ̂ᵢ`, (2.10) `n^{−1/2}λⁿ₀ → λ₀`,
(2.11) `n^{−1/2}(µⁿᵢ − nµᵢ) → µ̂ᵢ`, (2.12) `λᵢ = µᵢ`, and (2.13) `n^{1/2}Zⁿᵢ(0) → 0` in
probability. (`n^{−1/2}` is `1 / √n`; its value at `n = 0` is irrelevant to the limits.) -/
structure HeavyTraffic (S : LoadBalancingSequence Ω N) where
  lam : Fin N → ℝ
  lamHat : Fin N → ℝ
  lam0 : ℝ
  mu : Fin N → ℝ
  muHat : Fin N → ℝ
  lam_pos : ∀ i, 0 < lam i
  lam0_pos : 0 < lam0
  mu_pos : ∀ i, 0 < mu i
  /-- (2.9) -/
  tendsto_lamHat : ∀ i, Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => ((S.lam n i : ℝ) - n * lam i) / Real.sqrt n)
    atTop (𝓝 (lamHat i))
  /-- (2.10) -/
  tendsto_lam0Hat : Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => (S.lam0 n : ℝ) / Real.sqrt n) atTop (𝓝 lam0)
  /-- (2.11) -/
  tendsto_muHat : ∀ i, Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => (S.mu n i - n * mu i) / Real.sqrt n)
    atTop (𝓝 (muHat i))
  /-- (2.12) -/
  critical : ∀ i, lam i = mu i
  /-- (2.13) -/
  residual : ∀ i, TendstoInMeasure S.P (fun (n : ℕ) ω => Real.sqrt n * S.Z n i 0 ω) atTop
    (fun _ => 0)

/-- `X̂ⁿ(0−) = n^{−1/2} Xⁿ(0−)` (p. 6). -/
noncomputable def Xhat0 (S : LoadBalancingSequence Ω N) (n : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : Fin N → ℝ :=
  fun i => (S.X0m n i ω : ℝ) / Real.sqrt n

/-- **(IC₀)** (p. 6): `X̂ⁿ(0−) ⇒ X₀`, i.e. the laws of `X̂ⁿ(0−)` converge weakly to the law
`μ₀` of `X₀` (an `ℝ^N_+`-valued random vector; nonnegativity of `μ₀` follows). -/
def IC0 (S : LoadBalancingSequence Ω N) (μ₀ : ProbabilityMeasure (Fin N → ℝ)) : Prop :=
  ∃ ν : ℕ → ProbabilityMeasure (Fin N → ℝ),
    (∀ n, (ν n : Measure (Fin N → ℝ)) = S.P.map (Xhat0 S n)) ∧ Tendsto ν atTop (𝓝 μ₀)

/-- The service-time standard deviation `σᵢ^ser = (∫ (x − 1)² dΦ^ser_i)^{1/2}` (mean `1`). -/
noncomputable def serviceSD (S : LoadBalancingSequence Ω N) (i : Fin N) : ℝ :=
  Real.sqrt (∫ x, (x - 1) ^ 2 ∂(S.Φser i))

/-- The data (2.17): `b_r = λ₀ p_r`. -/
def driftB {S : LoadBalancingSequence Ω N} (H : HeavyTraffic S) : Fin N → ℝ :=
  fun r => H.lam0 * S.p r

/-- The data (2.17): `mᵢ = λ̂ᵢ − µ̂ᵢ`. -/
def driftM {S : LoadBalancingSequence Ω N} (H : HeavyTraffic S) : Fin N → ℝ :=
  fun i => H.lamHat i - H.muHat i

/-- The data (2.17): `σᵢ = (λᵢ + µᵢ (σᵢ^ser)²)^{1/2}`. -/
noncomputable def diffSigma {S : LoadBalancingSequence Ω N} (H : HeavyTraffic S) : Fin N → ℝ :=
  fun i => Real.sqrt (H.lam i + H.mu i * serviceSD S i ^ 2)

/-- (2.14): `X̂ⁿᵢ(t) = n^{−1/2} Xⁿᵢ(t)`. -/
noncomputable def Xhat (S : LoadBalancingSequence Ω N) (n : ℕ) (ω : Ω) (t : ℝ) : Fin N → ℝ :=
  fun i => S.X n i ω t / Real.sqrt n

/-- (2.14): `L̂ⁿᵢ(t) = n^{−1/2} µⁿᵢ (t − Tⁿᵢ(t))`, the scaled cumulative idle time. -/
noncomputable def Lhat (S : LoadBalancingSequence Ω N) (n : ℕ) (ω : Ω) (t : ℝ) : Fin N → ℝ :=
  fun i => S.mu n i * (t - S.T n i ω t) / Real.sqrt n

end RankBasedSDI.LoadBalancing


